  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 3,
      "comment": "Mix ingredients except vitamin solution, sulfur and Na2S·9H2O, and adjust pH to 7. Autoclave under a N2 atmosphere. Filter-sterilize vitamin solution. Sulfur is sterilized separately by autoclaving for 60 min at 105℃ on each of 3 successive days. Neutralize Na2S·9H2O as 5% solution and autoclave under a N2 atmosphere. Prior to inoculation, aseptically and anaerobically add vitamin, sulfur and Na2S·9H2O."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 4,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 6,
      "comment": ""
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 7,
      "comment": "Dissolve nitrilotriacetic acid and adjust pH to 6.5 with KOH solution. Then proceed to add minerals. Adjust final pH to 7.0."
    },
    {
      "paragraph_index": 8,
      "comment": ""
    }
  ]
}